{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>You shall not follow the majority to do evil.</b> To tilt the verdict toward guilt in capital cases, for one does not convict on the testimony of a single judge alone." "<b>And you shall not answer regarding a dispute.</b> When your fellow judges ask you what is your opinion." "<b>To incline after the majority.</b> Your answer shall not be that it is proper to incline after the majority, if ten acquit and the eleventh convicts." "<b>To pervert.</b> So as to tilt the verdict through your word toward guilt, so that there would then be twelve convicting. Rather, state your opinion and your reasoning. It shall not suffice you to say that it is proper to incline after the opinion of the majority without offering any reasoning for it other than that they outnumber those who acquit, and that a conviction requires a majority of two."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:53.748272480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}